  "title": "Yield Not Thy Core",
  "abstract": "Programming distributed systems has never been easier, but making them perform well and efficiently exploit available resources remains difficult. Fast programs on a single host slow to a crawl when given more resources, while systems designed for scale squander resources on modest problems.",
